## Why This Is Asked

Addresses real-world needs for analytics while protecting sensitive SAP data. Evaluates understanding of data masking, per-tenant access control, and end-to-end data lineage.

## Key Concepts

- SAP data export pipelines to data lakes
- Field-level masking for PII/financial data
- Deterministic masking to preserve join feasibility
- IAM SCPs and per-tenant roles for isolation
- Data lineage via Glue Data Catalog
- KMS encryption at rest; minimal IaC for keys/roles

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: deterministic mask preserving format
function maskForColumn(val){ 
  if (val===null) return null;
  const s = String(val);
  const masked = s.replace(/[0-9]/g,'0');
  return masked.length>0 ? masked : val;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotence and integrity after multiple masking runs?
- What strategies ensure masking policies stay in sync with SAP authorization changes?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests end-to-end observability design for SAP on AWS, tying SAP metrics to AWS cost and performance signals, and validating the candidate's ability to implement a data plane, anomaly detection, and dashboards.

## Key Concepts
- SAP ABAP latency & HANA wait events
- OpenTelemetry + CloudWatch + S3
- SageMaker anomaly detection
- Lambda metric emission & custom metrics
- Cost-aware dashboards (QuickSight)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Lambda to emit a CloudWatch metric
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const cw = new AWS.CloudWatch();
exports.handler = async () => {
  const latency = await pingSAPAndMeasureLatency();
  await cw.putMetricData({
    Namespace: 'SAP/Observability',
    MetricData: [
      { MetricName: 'ABAP_RPC_Latency_ms', Value: latency, Unit: 'Milliseconds' }
    ]
  }).promise();
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you minimize SAP-instrumentation overhead?
- How would you validate the anomaly model against real incidents?
